    "title": "Booker T Comments On Powerhouse Hobbs Joining WWE - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anthony Nash ,\n2 hours ago Photo Credit: AEW Powerhouse Hobbs is set to start his WWE career shortly, and according to Booker T, he thinks he’ll fit right in.\nSpeaking during the latest episode of his Hall of Fame podcast (via WrestlingNews.co ), Booker T said he thinks Hobbs will fit right in. He also said he’s been pushing for Hobbs to get to WWE for some time now.\n“Will Hobbs is a guy that I’ve been pushing for for quite some time. As far as this guy, all he needs is a shot and an opportunity, and he definitely can, you know, take this business by storm,” Booker T said. “I tell you a little story about Will Hobbs, you know, show up at the arenas, show up at the arenas, and Will would be there waiting, you know, Uncle Book, let me holler. And, you know, he would always run up on me. And man would always talk, and I would always give Will, you know, advice, because he said, I’m trying, man, I’m trying to get in. Man, who did I talk to?”\nBooker T thinks Hobbs will be a good addition Booker T went on to note he would give Hobbs some advice on always persisting and continuing to chase his dream. Now, Booker T says, he’s proud to see the man he’s become, and welcomes him into the WWE for what he believes will be “a fitting addition.”\n“I say, bro. You know, it’s just not like that. I say, but trust me, just keep doing what you’re doing, and don’t stop. And trust me, it’s gonna happen for you. And then, boom, he shows up in AEW and becomes Powerhouse Hobbs, and the rest is history.\n“I look at the growth of Will Hobbs, as far as just the evolution of Hobbs, you know, from that kid I was talking to, to this grown man that’s out there, that’s beast as most that’s out there right now, talking about no bread, no water, just meat, that this dude Will Hobbs. So no, I’m looking forward to if he does make that step over to the WWE, I think he’ll be a fitting addition. I think he’ll fit right in, and I think he’ll make money moves right off the bat.”\nREAD MORE: AEW Dynamite Results: Review, Grades, Card For Jan 21\nThe post Booker T Comments On Powerhouse Hobbs Joining WWE appeared first on Wrestlezone .",
